<!-- Definition and symptoms -->
'''Neural tube defects''' ('''NTDs''') are a group of [[birth defects]] in which an opening in the [[Vertebral column|spine]] or [[cranium]] remains from early in human development. In the third week of pregnancy called [[gastrulation]], specialized cells on the dorsal side of the embryo begin to change shape and form the [[neural tube]]. When the neural tube does not close completely, an NTD develops.

<!-- Cause -->
Specific types include: [[spina bifida]] which affects the [[Human vertebral column|spine]], [[anencephaly]] which results in little to no [[brain]], [[encephalocele]] which affects the [[skull]], and [[iniencephaly]] which results in severe neck problems.<ref name=NIH2017Def/>

<!-- Epidemiology -->
NTDs are one of the most common [[birth defects]], affecting over 300,000 births each year worldwide.<ref>{{cite web |author=National Center on Birth Defects and Developmental Disabilities |title=Neural Tube Defects (Annual Report) |year=2012 |publisher=US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention |url=https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/aboutus/annualreport2012/documents/ar2012-folicacid-printversion.pdf}}</ref> For example, [[spina bifida]] affects approximately 1,500 births annually in the United States, or about 3.5 in every 10,000 (0.035% of US births),<ref name=NIH2017Def>{{cite web |publisher=National Institute of Child Health and Human Development, U.S. National Institutes of Health |title=Neural Tube Defects (NTDs): Condition Information |date=2017|url=https://www.nichd.nih.gov/health/topics/ntds/conditioninfo|access-date=30 November 2017}}</ref><ref name=CDC2017Sats>{{cite web |title=Spina Bifida - Data and Statistics |access-date=29 November 2017|publisher=National Center on Birth Defects and Developmental Disabilities, US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention |url=https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/spinabifida/data.html|date=12 October 2016}}</ref> which has decreased from around 5 per 10,000 (0.05% of US births) since [[#Prevention|folate fortification]] of grain products was started.<ref name=CDC2017Sats/> The number of deaths in the US each year due to neural tube defects also declined from 1,200 before folate fortification was started to 840.<ref name="folic-acid-global">{{cite web |author=National Center on Birth Defects and Developmental Disabilities |title=Folic Acid – Birth Defects Count |access-date=13 May 2014 |publisher=US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention |url=https://www.cdc.gov/ncbddd/folicacid/global.html}}</ref>

